   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### To what extent will the introduction of mandatory helmet requirement change the usage patterns towards helmet use?\n",
    "\n",
    "The introduction of the helmet mandate in 2023 for Dutch light moped (snorfiets) is utilized to make a forecast of change in usage patterns towards helmet use. The research towards attitude and the modal change effects could bring valuable insides for a new mandate for e-bikes.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Effect of a helmet mandate on underage e-bike use and road incidents\n",
    "\n",
    "A helmet mandate would raise helmet use very likely. However, it may also push many underage riders off the e-bike. The net effect on fatal and serious incidents is probably positive (Schmidt et al., 2026). The displaced trips move to slower modes rather than to faster vehicles since they have no legal alternative within the age range 12-17 years old.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Helmet usage pattern\n",
    "\n",
    "After the Dutch light moped (snorfiets) mandate of 1 January 2023, roadside counts found 99% helmet use (Schmidt et al., 2026). Among the riders who kept riding the light moped, those wearing a helmet \"always\" rose from 9% to 67% (Schmidt et al., 2026). Voluntary use among young cyclists is very low: 77.8% of 12–24-year-olds never wear a helmet, and only 0.4% do so on an e-bike (TeamAlert, 2020). Among e-bike and fatbike casualties at emergency departments, helmet use was 6% and 3% (VeiligheidNL, 2024)."
   ]
  },
