    "#### Attitudes of underage riders\n",
    "\n",
    "Young riders value the e-bike for speed and low effort. One rider named not having to wear a helmet as a reason to prefer it over a scooter (TeamAlert, 2023). Among 12–24-year-olds, 46.9% say others' opinions matter if they wear a helmet and 48.3% fear remarks (TeamAlert, 2020). In focus groups with 13–18-year-olds, nobody wore a helmet, some said they would stop riding an e-bike if one were required, and one said she would not wear it if she were the only one (TeamAlert, 2023). After the light moped mandate, 20% of surveyed riders stopped among those who continued, daily or weekly use fell from about three-quarters to just over half, 34% rode less and 15% later stopped (Schmidt et al., 2026). Attitudes improved among continuing riders: helmet use seen as a habit rose from 19.7% to 50.9%, and the perception that others wear helmets rose from 18.2% to 63.6% (Schmidt et al., 2026).\n",
    "\n"
