    "#### Where trips go\n",
    "\n",
    "Replaced light moped trips went mainly to cars (over 50%), e-bikes (33%), regular bicycles (20%) and walking (20%) fatbikes and speed pedelecs were chosen by fewer than 5% (Schmidt et al., 2026). The combined moped and light moped fleet fell by about 6%, with light mopeds down 24% and mopeds up 29% (Schmidt et al., 2026). Some young e-bike riders already tune their bikes to 32–37 km/h (TeamAlert, 2023), This means a move to faster or tuned vehicles is plausible, but the sources do not quantify it.\n",
    "\n"
