    "\n",
    "#### Forecast for fatal and serious incidents\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Direct effect:**\n",
    "\n",
    "  Helmets cut serious head injury risk by about 60% and fatal head trauma by 70% (TeamAlert, 2020). Among the seriously injured light moped riders, the part with severe head injury fell from 55% to 30% (Schmidt et al., 2026). Brain injury accounted for 22% of e-bike and 17% of fatbike casualties (VeiligheidNL, 2024).\n",
    "  \n",
    "- **Exposure effect:**\n",
    "\n",
    "  After the 2023 mandate, light moped crashes fell 38%, rider deaths 38% and severe injuries 50% (Schmidt et al., 2026).\n",
    "- **Net effect:**\n",
    "\n",
    "  SWOV projected that full bicycle helmet compliance would save about 85 lives and 2,500–2,600 serious injuries per year (SWOV, 2022) judge the net effect of the light moped mandate likely favourable, but some casualties may now occur on other modes and the size of that shift is unknown. A shift to faster vehicles would reduce the gain."
   ]
